problemStatement:
A developer wrote a simple counter but it doesn’t work. The plus button does nothing, and the minus button causes an error.

**Given component:**
```typescript
// counter.component.ts
export class CounterComponent {
  count = 0;

  increment() {
    this.count = this.count + 1;
  }

  decrement() {
    this.count = this.count - 1;
  }
}
```

**Broken template:**
```html
<button on-click="increment()">+</button>
<span>{{ count }}</span>
<button [click]="decrement()">-</button>
```

Identify the two errors and fix them so that clicking + increases the count, clicking – decreases it.

solutionCode:
// Fixed template:
<button (click)="increment()">+</button>
<span>{{ count }}</span>
<button (click)="decrement()">-</button>

// Explanation: event binding uses parentheses, not `on-` prefix, and not square brackets.
